From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:29:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] hexagonfs: mapped: report the write bit only when the
 file is writable

stat sets the owner write bit when this process can write the file
(faccessat with AT_EACCESS), not when the backing file's mode has it. A
file on a read only mount or in a read only sandbox stats 0444 again,
and a directory 0555, as before the write paths were added.

Signed-off-by: seilent <github@seilent.net>
---
 hexagonrpcd/hexagonfs_mapped.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hexagonrpcd/hexagonfs_mapped.c b/hexagonrpcd/hexagonfs_mapped.c
index 400800f..7596b15 100644
--- a/hexagonrpcd/hexagonfs_mapped.c
+++ b/hexagonrpcd/hexagonfs_mapped.c
@@ -19,6 +19,8 @@
  * along with this program.  If not, see <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.
  */
 
+#define _GNU_SOURCE
+
 #include <dirent.h>
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
@@ -339,7 +341,7 @@ static int mapped_stat(struct hexagonfs_fd *fd, struct stat *stats)
 	 * Claiming a write bit the backing file lacks makes the DSP take a
 	 * write path that can only fail.
 	 */
-	if (phys.st_mode & S_IWUSR)
+	if (faccessat(ctx->fd, "", W_OK, AT_EMPTY_PATH | AT_EACCESS) == 0)
 		stats->st_mode |= S_IWUSR;
 
 	stats->st_atim.tv_sec = phys.st_atim.tv_sec;
